  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Controls:

    \tWASD - Move

    \tMouse - Look Around

    \tLeft Shift
    - Sprint

    \tSpace - Jump

    \tE - Interact

    \tLeft Click - Use Item

    \tEscape
    - Pause




    How To Play:

    To win complete 20 days without your family
    or your community starving. Harvest crops and sell them to your community at
    the market or store them in the box by your house for your family.


    To plant
    a crop till the soil with a hoe, use a seed packet to plant then make sure to
    water it every day. Use the watering can to water them which can be filled by
    interacting with the green water tank. Seeds can be bought from the market


    Every
    day if the crop is watered it will move to the next stage. Crops don''t need
    to be watered if there is rain. Soil is darker if it is wet. Rain also fills
    up the water tank.  If there is no rain you can always buy water for your tank.


    To
    move to the next day interact with the door to your house but make sure everyone
    has enough food before proceeding.




    Drought Disaster:

    Sometimes droughts
    happen, during these rain won''t appear for a while. Certain crops also will
    require more water so make sure to check if their soil is darker. Use water wisely.


    Pest
    Disaster:

    Sometimes pests will attack your crops. To kill them use BT spray.
    To reduce the chance of them attacking a crop use neem oil. Both of these can
    be bought from the shop. Pests do glow slightly so keep an eye out.




    Seasons:

    The
    game has 4 seasons, all of them affect the chance of rain and disasters. Also
    everyone will need different amounts of food every day depending on the season.




    Crop
    Information:

    \tCowpea - Green seed packet. Harvest on stage 3 or 4 (green/yellow
    pods)

    \tSorghum - Yellow seed packet. Harvest on stage 3 (yellow grains)

    \tTomato
    - Red Packet. Harvest on stage 5 (red fruits)'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
